{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518074-mythic-memory","id":1518074,"title":"Mythic Memory","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-15T13:30:09-07:00","id":1518074,"title":"Mythic Memory","content":"In the spirit of cross-over material such as Blood Treachery, I am pondering whether Kindred being static creatures are unaffected by changes to reality and remember the mythic times of the Dark Ages and Sorcerers Crusade.<br /> <br /> The kindred like most Nightfolk possess innate magic resistance or counter magik, but this dosen\u2019t necessary protect their memory or recollection of dragons, unicorns or even the true fae.<br /> <br /> Or maybe it does\u2026<br /> <br /> My thinking is it might be connected to generation/blood potency, perhaps the ancient elders can remember despite the technocracies rewrites.<br /> <br /> What do people think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T13:37:21-07:00","id":1518075,"title":"","content":"While it\u2019s a bit of a fine touch, you have to balance how fantastical any group is willing to accept the past as having been, I usually assume that one of the reasons why elders come off so strangely to younger kindred is that they are more highly aware of fantastical threats and concerns which had been previously part of the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T13:52:15-07:00","id":1518078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518074-mythic-memory?p=1518075#post1518075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it\u2019s a bit of a fine touch, you have to balance how fantastical any group is willing to accept the past as having been, I usually assume that one of the reasons why elders come off so strangely to younger kindred is that they are more highly aware of fantastical threats and concerns which had been previously part of the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s a good point, you\u2019ve hit the nail on the head of my thought process.<br /> <br /> I was picturing whether a conversation between an ancient master of the technocracy and say Mithras or Helena, would work on the basis of the latter remembering the time before reason even though the history books and even their childer had no knowledge or recollection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T20:46:49-07:00","id":1518125,"title":"","content":"I would say ancient vampires do remember the past times when unicorns, griffins, fairies, giants, etc. were around. If they saw them and remembered them afterwards (meaning they did not succumb to anything like the Delerium, Fog, or Mists) than it is just another memory they have. They'd probably deduce the reason for they are no longer around for the same reasons &quot;magic&quot; declined. The world was once more magical. Now it isn't. That's why House Tremere became Clan Tremere. And the decline of magic is the basis for at least one Gehenna cult.<br /> <br /> But it's not like there still isn't a lot of supernatural creatures around in the modern age if they know what to look for - besides the classic game splats there are fomori and various monsters still out there.<br /> <br /> I would say the only things they wouldn't remember would be wholescale rewriting of history because of a massive Paradox backlash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T02:56:29-07:00","id":1518135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518074-mythic-memory?p=1518125#post1518125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now it isn't. That's why House Tremere became Clan Tremere. And the decline of magic is the basis for at least one Gehenna cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s an interesting point, one of the concepts from Blood Treachery is the Tremeres Blood Magic effectively countering Sphere Magik by virtue of it being derived from their original Hermetic principles, so it raises the possibility that the Tremere retain some other protection from memory rewrites etc <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518074-mythic-memory?p=1518125#post1518125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say the only things they wouldn't remember would be wholescale rewriting of history because of a massive Paradox backlash.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another interesting idea, as I started to think it through it came down to the idea that some elders might have retained memory of the original history by virtue of an innate resistance, strong blood, thaurmaturgy, being quasi mythic themselves, even unknowingly having dwelt or gone into Torpor in a non-scientific reality zone.<br /> <br /> Tremere Chantry\u2019s are reputed to be reality zones (in M20 terms) where magc(k) is coincidental.<br /> <br /> In game terms much of this is just background, after all how does it benefit an elder, but it raises some interesting possibilities Odin or Louhi having full recollection of true history and where remaining places or magic or artefacts might lie, an elders motivations for sending his childer into the astral plane.<br /> <br /> And particularly the Tremeres motives as to why they might come into conflict with non-kindred, although they decided to cheat their fate and become vampires - how might they use their retained knowledge and play with local reality to their benefit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}